.TH AX25CHK 1
.SH NAME
ax25chk \- check the ax25 device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ax25chk setup
.I call
.br
.B ax25chk send
.I call text
.RI [ count ]
.br
.B ax25chk sendvia
.I call path text
.br
.B ax25chk beacon
.I text
.br
.B ax25chk recv
.RI [ count ]
.br
.B ax25chk stats
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ax25chk
exercises
.IR ax25 (3)
from outside the kernel.
.PP
.B Setup
attaches
.B /dev/radio0/data
to
.B #a
and sets this station's callsign, then checks the things a shell cannot
reach: that a seventh callsign character and an SSID of 16 are refused,
that a conversation's
.B iounit
is 239 with no digipeaters and 225 with two, that a write past the
information field is refused naming the budget, that a third digipeater
is refused, and that the path may not change while
.B data
is open.  That last is the
.B iounit
being a promise rather than an estimate.
.PP
.B Beacon
sends one UI frame to
.BR QST ,
which is what a beacon is.
.B Sendvia
sends through a digipeater path.
.SH EXAMPLE
Two stations under a QEMU patched to model an SX1276.  On the first:
.PP
.EX
	ax25chk setup KA9Q-1
	ax25chk recv 2
.EE
.PP
and on the second,
.IR ax25raw (1)
building the frames by hand.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/ax25chk.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.I ax25raw (1),
.I ax25 (3),
.I lorachk (1)
.SH BUGS
Each invocation opens its own conversation and closes it on exit.
.PP
.B Setup
must run before anything else, and only once.
